    "body": "## Security impact\n\nSaving a job/bookmark is only valid for publicly available `OPEN` listings, but `SavedJobService.save()` previously loaded any numeric job ID globally and only then checked its lifecycle status. An authenticated outsider could therefore distinguish a nonexistent job (`404`) from an existing non-public job (`409`), creating an existence/lifecycle oracle for accepted, completed or cancelled jobs that are no longer part of public discovery.\n\n## Fix\n\n- add an `id + status` repository lookup and resolve bookmark writes directly as `findByIdAndStatus(jobId, OPEN)`;\n- return the existing neutral job-not-found response when the ID is missing **or** the listing is no longer public/open;\n- remove the post-load lifecycle branch, so a non-open private job is never materialized by the bookmark-write path;\n- preserve existing open-listing rules: users still cannot bookmark their own listing, block relationships still prevent bookmarking, and bookmark creation remains idempotent.\n\n`status`, batched statuses, remove and list remain user-scoped/idempotent and are unchanged.\n\n## Tests\n\n- existing successful/idempotent bookmark tests now exercise the open-scoped repository lookup;\n- regression coverage requires unavailable listings to resolve as not-found through the scoped lookup;\n- regression coverage explicitly verifies the legacy global `findById` path is not used and no bookmark lookup/write occurs after the neutral failure;\n- own-listing and block-policy behavior remains covered.\n\nNo schema, payment, escrow, routing, location, notification or public discovery behavior is changed.\n\n## Merge gate\n\nMerge only after all relevant checks on the exact PR head are green, revalidate that `master` has not moved (or safely rebase if needed), then merge with a merge commit using the exact checked head SHA. Verify post-merge master and workflows before starting another slice.",
